<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The place floor pin ~ a pin the quorum's act vouches for

A floor route takes its pin only through an authenticated relation or a carried signed pin set, and an
announcement never authenticates its own first pin (house ruling "The admit's gate pin"). A herm's floor pin
derives from its floor key, which no seat holds, so no seat can mint it. The relation that vouches for it is
the one the Nexus already published: the quorum's counted `carry` over the herm's vessel key.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-statement>>

!! The statement ~ one per place per Nexus

The place signs `{ kind, placeKey, nexus, route, tier, digest }` over the pin it stands at that Nexus, with
the key the quorum's act names (`PLACE_FLOOR_PIN_DOMAIN`, registered in `domains`, apart from every other seal). It rides
the Nexus's carriage board under a sidecar key apart from the acts (`PLACE_FLOOR_PIN_PREFIX`), which the act
extractor skips. Any replica writer may carry it; none can forge it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-reader>>

!! The reader files only what it can vouch for

`readPlaceFloorPin` refuses by name, never throws, and files only when all of these hold:

# the statement reads whole and its pin reads whole (`readGateBundlePin`), at FLOOR tier, at the Nexus the
reader asked, on the route asked;
# the signature verifies under `placeKey` over this exact image;
# LAST, the relation: the reader's OWN held root of that Nexus counts a `carry` for `placeKey`.

A key the reader's replica does not count authenticates nothing (`place-uncarried`). The index it files into
is the pair index (`admit-gate-pin`), keyed (place key, Nexus hex, route, tier).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-place-arm>>

!! The place arm

A place presents the quorum's counted `carry` act over its own key at the gate's Nexus, with every counted
act of that relation in its causal past as the lineage the gate's reader walks (`placeArmFor`,
`verifyPresentedCarry`). The head is the counted `carry` no other counted act of this place descends from; a
counted `uncarry` that descends from it leaves the place with no arm to present. A lineage past
`PLACE_LINEAGE_BOUND` presents nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/owed>>

!! Owed

The statement carries no causal position, and the pair index holds no replace by design: an older valid
statement can stand in for a newer one after a floor-key rotation until the index drops. Owed as one piece:
a position on the statement (the carrying roster's `sealEpochCid` and the place's own pin generation) and a
causal replace door on the index that reads it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

